      {
        "document_id": "pmid-25686603",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 377,
        "quote": "In a proliferation assay measuring tritiated thymidine incorporation in the presence of axitinib, Ba/F3 cells carrying the BCR-ABL1 variant showed decreased incorporation when harboring fusions with the V299L variant of ABL1 compared to fusions with wildtype ABL1 (IC50 of 188nM vs. 823 nM), indicating V299L induces sensitivity compared to BCR-ABL1 without secondary variants."
      }
    ],
